I must say, the dev team has produced a challenging new game in NetHack 3.1.3
but I have to speak my mind about these annoyances I have found.

* - The mac interface of putting everything in a pop-up-and-click window
was still left in. This, to me is QUITE ANNOYING, as I play NetHack
on a Mac Plus, with very little window space. I never had any trouble
with running or playing 3.09j and I liked the TTY interface. I really
wish this could have been kept fully. I know you can set this function
in the defaults file, and this brings up another gripe.

* - For those who may not be familiar with the language of writing
defaults, this was the only place I felt that a mac interface was
helpful, as it would be much easier to set a radio box than try and
figure out the semblance of writing it out.

Now, I must say, I find the game a GREAT challenge, bugs aside and I have
no problem with any of the nuances, except for a question. Why are
apes classified under Y(eti)? Shouldn't they be h(umanoids)?

And, a hypothetical question. If I was trapped inside a purple worm and
I intentionally pissed off my deity to the point of him zapping me,
shouldn't the lightning bolt/death beam kill the purple worm first? ;)

---------

Now, an idea for NetHack 3.1.4 or 3.2

A special designation in the Player Info to show gender
G:M or G:F or G:N for non-gender monsters. I did think it a cute
idea that only females of a monster species could lay eggs. ;)

